ICC color profiles are binary files that cannot be represented as text.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
 🎨  ASH DOTFILES v5.0 — COLOR PROFILE SETUP
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Download the official sRGB ICC profile from:

  Official ICC:
  https://www.color.org/sRGB_v4_ICC_preference.icc

  ICC v2 (broader compatibility):
  https://www.color.org/sRGB_IEC61966-2-1_black_scaled.icc

  Or copy from system:
  cp /usr/share/color/icc/colord/sRGB.icc ~/.config/color-profiles/sRGB.icc
  cp /usr/share/color/icc/sRGB.icc ~/.config/color-profiles/sRGB.icc

Place the binary file at:
  ~/.config/color-profiles/sRGB.icc

Then assign via:
  colormgr — GNOME/KDE color management daemon
  icc-profiles — system-wide ICC profiles
  hyprland: monitor color_profile = ~/.config/color-profiles/sRGB.icc

ASH integration:
  ash theme colors --profile sRGB